# plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md §6 V2a: YO_AUDIT_INOUT_BORROW lists every write
# that the collections-become-values flip (V2b) would change, without failing:
# a write through a by-value parameter or a `match`/`for` binding (as an
# `inout` receiver, an `inout` argument or an assignment into the place), a
# callee whose mutation mask is unresolved (`-unresolved`), and a write to a
# closure's capture (`-capture`). Writes through a local, an `inout`
# parameter or a `Box` are not listed. Since the flip (B8) two of the listed
# shapes are unrepresentable: a value list written through a `match` binding
# of a map value is E0901 (the read copies a move-only value), and a write to
# a value `for` binding is E0917; the fixture keeps an owned `get_cloned` copy
# as a not-listed row in their place.
env=YO_AUDIT_INOUT_BORROW=1
stdout_keep_match=\[inout-borrow[a-z-]*\] main\.yo:[0-9]+:[0-9]+
timeout=120
